<description>
The function `Strnew_m_charp` is a variadic function that concatenates a variable number of C-style strings into a single `Str` object. It takes a variable number of `const char *` arguments, with the list of arguments terminated by a `NULL` pointer. The function initializes a new `Str` object and then iterates through the provided string arguments, appending each one to the new `Str` object until a `NULL` argument is encountered.
</description>

<requirements>
<requirement>
The variadic argument list must be terminated by a NULL pointer. This is because the function iterates through the arguments until it encounters a NULL, so a missing terminator will lead to a crash.
</requirement>
<requirement>
Each non-NULL argument in the variadic argument list must be a pointer to a null-terminated string. This is because the function uses `strlen` to determine the length of each string, and a non-null-terminated string will cause `strlen` to read out of bounds.
</requirement>
</requirements>

